config HAR_INFERENCE_POSTPROCESSING
	bool "Apply inference postprocessing before publishing"
	default n
	help
	  When enabled, classification output is stabilized by requiring a
	  per-class number of consecutive identical predictions before being
	  logged, shown on the LED, and sent over BLE.

	  When disabled, every raw model prediction is logged and published.

config HAR_POSTPROCESSING_PUBLISH_TIMEOUT_MS
	int "Maximum time without a published classification [ms]"
	depends on HAR_INFERENCE_POSTPROCESSING
	range 1000 60000
	default 8000
	help
	  While the activity changes, the raw prediction may keep alternating so
	  that no class ever reaches its repeat count and nothing is published.
	  Once this time has passed without any output, the class predicted most
	  often since the last published result is published instead.

	  The gap is bounded by this value plus one inference period, because the
	  timeout is only evaluated when a new raw prediction arrives.

	  Lower values shorten the worst-case gap but force a guess while the
	  model is still undecided, which costs accuracy. Replaying the captured
	  test logs gives 81.2% at 3 s, 87.6% at 5 s, 89.9% at 8 s and 90.9% with
	  the fallback disabled entirely, the last at the price of a 17.9 s gap.

config HAR_LOG_RAW_PREDICTIONS
	bool "Also report every raw prediction, before post-processing"
	depends on HAR_INFERENCE_POSTPROCESSING
	help
	  When enabled, every model output is reported with a "RAW," prefix in
	  addition to the results that postprocessing decides to publish. Both
	  line types carry the same fields, so a recording can be analysed as a
	  raw prediction stream, as a published stream, or as both.

	  Postprocessing publishes only once a class repeats, which correlates
	  with the model being right, so a recording that contains published
	  results alone gives an optimistic view of the model and no way to
	  reconstruct what it actually predicted. Reporting the raw stream as
	  well makes model accuracy and published accuracy measurable from the
	  same recording, and lets different repeat counts be evaluated by
	  replaying the recording offline.

	  Costs one extra log line and BLE message per inference period.

config BLE_NUS_OUTPUT
	bool "Send classification results over BLE NUS"
	depends on BT
	select BT_NUS
	select BT_DIS
	select BT_DIS_PNP
	select BT_BAS
	help
	  When enabled, recognized activity class and probability are sent as
	  text over the Nordic UART Service whenever the classification changes.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
